<title>RUSSIA: Russian 294-day T-bill yields 30.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 294-day T-bill yields 30.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 294-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 30.71 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had expected the yield to be between 29.9 and 32.0 percent.</p>
<p>The 22072 series bills, maturing on November 26, 1997, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed at 29.80 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Both issues are subject to a new 15-percent tax on government securities. Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number			     22074</p>
<p>    Issue volume				7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			    9.21 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)			    5.78 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				    4.63 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			    80.17 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		  80.04 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			    30.71 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		 30.96 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor					 294 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			     Dec 10, 1997</p>
<p>On February 19, the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles ($705.7 million) of 168-day T-bills (series 22073).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 7.52 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22043).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5668 Russian Roubles)</p>
